    watch: 'HR certificates without any data or process proof rarely change interview outcomes.',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Operations and business analytics BBA',
    title: 'The fastest lane to a tool-led role',
    core: 'Process thinking and reporting',
    multiplier: 'SQL, Power BI, and a project management basics course',
    proof: 'A report that finds a cost or delay problem in a public dataset and proposes a fix',
    watch: 'Learning five tools at a shallow level is worse than one tool with a finished project.',
  },
];

const checkpointItems = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Biology: how you work best',
    body: 'Do you focus best on long exam preparation (CS, CMA, CA, CFA), on building things and reports (Excel, SQL, Power BI), or on people-facing work (sales, marketing, HR)? Pick a course that matches the kind of effort you can sustain for months.',
    note: 'A course that fights your energy pattern will not survive its second month.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Context: your college, money and year',
    body: 'A first-year student can afford a slow, deep skill. A final-year student needs one visible proof before placements. If your family income is tight, choose the cheapest route that still produces proof, and skip anything that needs a loan.',
    note: 'The plan your household can fund end to end beats the plan with the louder name.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Market: what real job posts ask for',
    body: 'Open ten fresher job posts for the role you want on Naukri or LinkedIn. Note which tools and credentials repeat. Excel, SQL and CRM tools show up far more often than a specific certificate name.',
