];

const gateItems = [
  {
    num: 'Gate 1',
    title: 'Proof of skill',
    body: 'Before paying, finish one small piece of work from free material: a dashboard, a model, a mock campaign, or a mock paper. If you cannot get through the free version, a paid version will not fix that.',
  },
  {
    num: 'Gate 2',
    title: 'Proof of communication',
    body: 'Explain your piece of work in two minutes to a senior, a family friend in business, or a mentor. If it does not make sense out loud, it will not make sense in an interview.',
  },
  {
    num: 'Gate 3',
    title: 'Proof of value',
    body: 'Show it to three people who already work in that role and ask what is missing. One useful correction is worth more than another certificate.',
  },
];

const mistakeItems = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Collecting certificates in the first year instead of finishing one project',
    body: 'Employers screen for something you can walk them through. A folder of eight badges with no project looks like eight weekends of watching videos.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Paying a lakh for a "job-guarantee" bundle before testing the subject free',
    body: 'Sample the subject through free YouTube playlists, NPTEL and official learning paths first. Check the last update date, the syllabus, and what graduates of that exact course actually do now.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Choosing a college and then assuming its add-on course covers the tool gap',
    body: 'Many BBA syllabi still treat Excel and data as a light subject. AICTE itself has said BBA, BCA and BMS syllabi had not been revised for over 20 years, and has been rolling out a new model curriculum with internships since 2024-25.',
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    title: 'Going for an MBA only because nothing else felt clear',
    body: 'A weak-proof profile does not become strong because the degree is more expensive. If your only reason is that you are not sure what to do, spend a stretch of time on proof first.',
  },
  {
    num: '05',
    title: 'Starting CA or CFA on impulse and quitting after the first attempt',
    body: 'These are multi-year plans. Try one mock paper and read the syllabus before you register, not after.',
  },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'What are the best courses for BBA students?',
    a: 'For most BBA students the best first course is not a certificate but a tool floor: Excel, SQL and Power BI, built into one finished project. After that, choose by your specialisation: NISM or CFA Level 1 for finance, Google Analytics and one ad platform for marketing, and people-data basics for HR. After graduation the real professional options are CS Executive, CMA, CA, CFA or an MBA from a strong institute. None of them is automatically best, and each one should pass a small free test before you pay.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which certification course is best to do along with BBA?',
    a: 'Pick the one that matches the role you want, and finish a project inside it. Google Data Analytics suits business analyst and operations paths. Google Digital Marketing and E-commerce suits marketing paths. NISM certification suits finance desks that SEBI regulates. A certificate helps most when it comes with one dashboard, model or campaign you can explain in an interview.',
