  {
    q: 'Can I do CA after BBA?',
    a: 'Yes. Graduates can register for CA Intermediate directly under ICAI\'s direct entry route. Coaching sites report the required marks as 55% for commerce graduates and 60% for other graduates, and a BBA is often treated in the second group. Confirm your own band on the ICAI portal before you plan around it. Plan for a multi-year commitment including articleship, and try a mock paper first.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can a BBA graduate do CS directly?',
    a: 'Yes. Graduates from any stream can register for CS Executive without clearing CSEET. Reported 2026 figures are about Rs 23,900 for Executive registration and Rs 1,500 per exam group. Fees change, so check the ICSI site before you pay.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is CMA a good option after BBA?',
    a: 'It can be, especially for finance-track BBA students who like costing, budgeting and business numbers. Direct entry to Intermediate exists for eligible graduates, but coaching guides warn against assuming every degree qualifies automatically, so read the current ICMAI prospectus. It usually costs less than CA and leads to controller and FP&A roles.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is MBA compulsory after BBA?',
    a: 'No. Many BBA graduates work first in analyst, sales, operations, HR or finance-support roles and add credentials later. An MBA makes sense when a specific strong institute and a specific target role need it. CAT 2026 is on 29 November 2026 and its registration has already closed, so the next realistic window for most students is the CAT cycle that opens around August next year. Check the official CAT website for the latest dates.',
  },
  {
    q: 'BBA or BCom: which needs fewer extra courses?',
    a: 'Neither degree is a finished skill set. BBA gives management basics and presentation practice; BCom gives deeper accounting and tax. A BBA student usually needs the tool floor and one domain skill; a BCom student usually needs the tool floor and communication. The detailed comparison is in our BBA vs BCom guide.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do online courses like Google or Coursera certificates get BBA students hired?',
    a: 'Not on their own. Google says 75% of its Digital Marketing certificate graduates report a positive career outcome within six months, but that figure is self-reported and comes from the company itself. What hiring managers respond to is the project you built while learning. Use the certificate as a structured path and treat the capstone as your real product.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are free courses enough for a BBA student?',
    a: 'For tools like Excel, SQL and Power BI, often yes: free YouTube playlists, official learning paths and NPTEL courses cover most of the content. What paid programmes can add is feedback, deadlines, live practice or a credential a target employer genuinely asks for. Pay only for the part you cannot get free.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I check if my BBA college is approved?',
    a: 'From the 2024-25 academic year, colleges offering BBA, BMS and BCA were brought under AICTE approval. Look for your college on the AICTE approved-institutes listing and confirm its university affiliation before you pay fees.',
